Translation patch: `Params::into_values` (loops, `sort_unstable`, `first`/`last`)

Change:
  - `for (i, _) in named_params.iter().enumerate().filter(|(_, x)| **x == name) { .. if first.is_none() { first = Some(i) } else { values[i] = value.clone() } }` becomes `let mut i = 0; while i < named_params.len() { if *named_params[i] == *name { .. match first { None => first = Some(i), Some(_) => values[i] = value.clone() } } i += 1; }`.
  - `indexes.sort_unstable(); match indexes.into_iter().enumerate().find(|x| x.0 != x.1) { Some((missing, _)) => Err(named_params[missing]), None => match named_params.last() { Some(last) => Err(last), None => Ok(values) } }` becomes `sort_indexes(&mut indexes)` (a new in-crate insertion sort on `&mut [usize]`), then `let mut missing = 0; while missing < indexes.len() && indexes[missing] == missing { missing += 1 }` and `if missing < indexes.len() { Err(named_params[missing]) } else if !named_params.is_empty() { Err(named_params[named_params.len() - 1]) } else { Ok(values) }`.
  - In the `Params::Empty` arm, `if let Some(first) = params.first()` becomes `if !params.is_empty()` with `params[0]`.
Why: Aeneas does not model `Enumerate`, `Filter`, `find`, closures, `slice::sort_unstable`, `first`/`last` or `Option::is_none` (patches 04/05/27).
Behaviour: Identical:
  - the same indices are visited in increasing order, and `Vec<u8> == Vec<u8>` is the comparison of the two byte slices;
  - sorting a `[usize]` ascending has a unique result, so the insertion sort leaves `indexes` exactly as `sort_unstable` would (it is O(n^2) instead of O(n log n));
  - `find` returns the first `k` with `indexes[k] != k`, which is the `missing` the scan stops at (`missing < indexes.len()` iff `find` returned `Some`);
  - `first()`/`last()` are `Some(&v[0])`/`Some(&v[len - 1])` exactly when `v` is non-empty.

